                                    <h2>Skincare specialist vs generic influencer agency</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Skincare specialist:</strong> Deep skincare creator network + derm + esthetician + concern-specific fluency. Higher fee + smaller scale. Right for concern-led + clinical brands.</p><p><strong>Category-broad D2C with skincare depth:</strong> ITD has 4+ published skincare case studies + broad D2C creator network + skincare-specific programme design. Balanced fluency + scale.</p><p><strong>Generic creator agency:</strong> Applies generic playbooks without skincare compliance + derm network + concern-content. Wrong for skincare.</p>
                                    <h2>Realistic budget for skincare influencer</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Growth-tier monthly budget:</strong> Rs 1.5-6 lakh / month all-in (creator fees + gifted product + rights + agency management).</p><p><strong>Deliverable volume:</strong> 20-40 creator posts / month across tiers + 4-8 macro Reels + 1-2 celebrity engagements / quarter.</p><p><strong>Expected ROI:</strong> 3-8x ROAS on amplification. 30-50% CPL reduction on retargeting using UGC. Derm content drives 40-60% higher conversion for clinical brands.</p>
                                    <h2>ITD skincare influencer approach</h2>
